                             'the added vocabulary and is\n'
                             '    applied only to text no request wrote, to find the '
                             'added tokens the template\n'
                             '    spelled. ``ordinary`` has no added vocabulary at all '
                             '(the Rust frontend calls\n'
                             '    this ``encode_ordinary``) and encodes the text '
                             'between those tokens, so text\n'
                             '    the request wrote can only become ordinary '
                             'vocabulary. Cutting only at the\n'
                             "    template's added tokens is exactly how the tokenizer "
                             'itself segments text,\n'
                             '    so a prompt whose request text spells no added token '
                             'encodes to the ids the\n'
                             '    whole string always did.\n'
                             '    """\n'
